The narrowed rule exposed two separate costs: recursive re-sorting of an already canonical eight-entry local scope, and reduction through `Option.getD` wrappers. I’m replacing the local proof representation with the exact canonical key order produced by the frozen insertion model, then unfolding only the specific generated hook needed by each premise. This preserves the same map value while sharply reducing elaboration.
